* SSZ vs RLP
** RLP (execution layer)
*** Length prefixes, no types
*** Canonical decoder rules
*** Schema lives in the client
*** Commitment: keccak over bytes, MPT
** SSZ (consensus layer)
*** Fixed part plus offsets
*** Little-endian, no self-description
*** Vectors, lists, bitfields, containers
*** Limit shapes the tree
left side
** hash_tree_root
*** Chunks, padding, length mix-in
*** Subtree caching: 39 hashes per update
*** Same bytes can share a root
** Measured on one mainnet block
*** SSZ 21% larger on transactions
*** Calldata: SSZ wins on withdrawals
*** Read: 296 against 4,102 gas
** Direction of travel
*** EIP-7688 scheduled for Glamsterdam
*** Progressive types come with it
*** SSZ transactions and receipts: Draft, unscheduled
*** EIP-7807 declined for Hegota
